text	**#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The task is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  I have not started the work yet. The take-in check found this:  ``` #91: branch fix/91-typo, 0 commits ahead of main, last commit 2026-11-03T00:00:00Z ```  A branch `fix/91-typo` is linked to the issue, but the issue has no assignee and no `in progress` label. GitHub does not record who made a branch, so it can be someone else's work.  **Is `fix/91-typo` your work or someone else's?** If it is someone else's, I will stop here. If it is yours, I will next ask if the work runs somewhere else or should continue here.
