text	I fixed **#91 README: the install command says npm instal** and pushed the fix, but I could not open the pull request: `gh pr create` failed.  **Change:** - `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop` instead of `npm instal shop`.  **Steps done:** - I assigned #91 to you and put the `in progress` label on it. The label did not exist in the repository, so the script created it. - I did the work in a new worktree on the linked branch `fix/91-typo`, at `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-typo`. - The tracker has no duplicates, no open bugs or debt on the same code, and no open PRs on it. - Commit `98a98e3` (`docs: fix the npm install command in the README`) is on `origin/fix/91-typo`. The repository is public, and the commit holds no private text.  **Check:** The repository has no check command: no `package.json`, no `Makefile` and no CI. Instead, I searched the tree for `instal` and found no match.  **Review:** This change is documents only, so it got one round. A review subagent read `9ad68aa..98a98e3` and found no defects and no nits. It could not confirm that the package is really named `shop`, because the tree holds only the README. The other steps of the review do not apply to a README-only change. The project has no `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, so the architecture review did not run; `craft:architecture` can write the first one.  **Docs:** `README.md` is the change itself.  **The blocker:** `gh pr create` stopped with this error: ``` fake gh: no answer for: pr create --assignee @me --base main --head fix/91-typo --title docs: fix the npm install command in the README --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ``` The `gh` here appears to be a stub that does not support this command. The rules say not to do the step another way after a failure, so the PR is not open and I have not asked the merge question. The PR description, with its `## Review` section, is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`. When `gh` works, run this from the worktree:  ```bash gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --head fix/91-typo \   --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  The issue keeps its `in progress` label and the worktree stays until the PR merges.
